# Fix similar findings together

When a problem is pointed out, do not fix only the cited spot and stop. Before fixing, check whether the same kind of gap exists elsewhere.

- Look in the same file, in callees with the same contract, and in the paired code: the offline verifier and the floating server, the on-premises server and the hosted service, checkout and renewal, the Windows, Linux, and macOS machine ID readers, the JIT and NativeAOT builds.
- Examples: an expiry compared with the wall clock in the verifier and the same comparison in the server; a request field that the signature does not cover on checkout and the same field on check-in; an unbounded read of a token file and the same read of a key file.
- If you find the same kind of problem, fix it together with the cited spot.
- If you find none, say what you checked and that nothing remains.
